        556.5198974609375,
        559.0498657226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1) Cluttered Environments: The first distribution of envi-",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399719238281,
        561.7213134765625,
        563.0349731445312,
        570.6278686523438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ronments consisted of randomly placed circular obstacles with",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        573.5573120117188,
        563.0353393554688,
        582.4638671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "random radii. These obstacles were allowed to overlap, which",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        585.393310546875,
        563.0355224609375,
        594.2998657226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "allowed the constraint regions to combine to form complex",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        597.2293090820312,
        563.0354614257812,
        606.1358642578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "environments. 100 testing environments were sampled from",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        609.0643310546875,
        563.0355224609375,
        617.9708862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "this distribution. Trivial environments in which no obstacles",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        620.9002685546875,
        563.0352783203125,
        629.8068237304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "blocked the path to the goal were discarded.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        632.736328125,
        494.2635192871094,
        641.6428833007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Results are shown in Table II, with an example environment",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399719238281,
        644.4432983398438,
        563.0350341796875,
        653.349853515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in Figure 5. When using a quadratic terminal cost, the system",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        656.2783203125,
        563.035400390625,
        665.1848754882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "often got caught in local minima. When using A*, the system",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        668.1143188476562,
        563.035400390625,
        677.0208740234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "occasionally planned paths through obscured obstacles, which",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        679.9503173828125,
        563.0354614257812,
        688.8568725585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "caused constraint violations if the LiDAR was unable to view",
